<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Evaluation Metrics</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report four evaluation metrics to assess the model’s performance.
Let <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> denote the total number of samples, <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> the set of ground-truth harmful samples, and <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the model’s prediction for sample <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(1) Classification Accuracy.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This metric measures the overall correctness of harmless/harmful classification across all samples:</p>
<table id="A4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Acc}_{\text{cls}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{cls}}=y_{i}^{\text{cls}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>cls</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Acc}_{\text{cls}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{cls}}=y_{i}^{\text{cls}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}^{\text{cls}}\in\{\text{harmless},\text{harmful}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>harmless</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>harmful</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}^{\text{cls}}\in\{\text{harmless},\text{harmful}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(2) Harmful Detection Precision.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This metric is restricted to the ground-truth harmful subset (<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in H</annotation></semantics></math>), and evaluates whether the model correctly identifies them as harmful:</p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Acc}_{\text{harm}}=\frac{1}{|H|}\sum_{i\in H}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{cls}}=\text{harmful}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>harm</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mtext>harmful</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Acc}_{\text{harm}}=\frac{1}{|H|}\sum_{i\in H}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{cls}}=\text{harmful}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(3) Risk Category Accuracy.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once a sample is correctly detected as harmful, we further evaluate whether the predicted risk label matches the ground-truth risk label <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}^{\text{risk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}^{\text{risk}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote this subset as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\text{det}}=\{i\in H\mid\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{cls}}=\text{harmful}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>det</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mtext>harmful</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\text{det}}=\{i\in H\mid\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{cls}}=\text{harmful}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Acc}_{\text{risk}}=\frac{1}{|H^{\text{det}}|}\sum_{i\in H^{\text{det}}}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{risk}}=y_{i}^{\text{risk}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>risk</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>det</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>det</mtext></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Acc}_{\text{risk}}=\frac{1}{|H^{\text{det}}|}\sum_{i\in H^{\text{det}}}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{risk}}=y_{i}^{\text{risk}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(4) Explanation Correctness.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the cases where the risk category is correctly predicted, we assess whether the model’s explanation semantically aligns with the ground-truth explanation <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}^{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}^{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is determined by an LLM-based judge returning a binary decision. Let <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\text{risk}}=\{i\in H^{\text{det}}\mid\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{risk}}=y_{i}^{\text{risk}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>det</mtext></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\text{risk}}=\{i\in H^{\text{det}}\mid\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{risk}}=y_{i}^{\text{risk}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Acc}_{\text{exp}}=\frac{1}{|H^{\text{risk}}|}\sum_{i\in H^{\text{risk}}}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\text{Judge}(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{exp}},y_{i}^{\text{exp}})=1\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mtext>risk</mtext></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Judge</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Acc}_{\text{exp}}=\frac{1}{|H^{\text{risk}}|}\sum_{i\in H^{\text{risk}}}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\text{Judge}(\hat{y}_{i}^{\text{exp}},y_{i}^{\text{exp}})=1\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Risk Definition</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show the definition of different risk types in <a href="#A5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix E Risk Definition ‣ Building a Foundational Guardrail for General Agentic Systems via Synthetic Data" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
